{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788474946289117333,"compiled_state":{"alias":"brunette-bellicose-blacklemur","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"26bde50ef298e3372a71d40cb6a5cc385c82bcdb9d90a30c4595a2eb660f375d","event_uuid":"518aa08c-6903-4ea4-8f01-087d1bf2136b","position":{"commit_sha":"24daaaf8893f2fd8c9c11c7961d1dd5e3d079a2d","position":"1788474258154670222-518aa08c-6903-4ea4-8f01-087d1bf2136b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"52fa0768876be9b29acbde0fe9d0272cdba55bed21ea6a784fd10a3168fe9e03","event_uuid":"72f618b9-44ac-44b9-b9a0-62258becfb38","position":{"commit_sha":"a8f4ecc6aabd56310dc982584d2df2b01255bfb0","position":"1788474317840715157-72f618b9-44ac-44b9-b9a0-62258becfb38"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"335822ad24edfdd01419264a8b1416891cbd6706b8a659fc9c162fbccd5c0f3e","event_uuid":"15d974be-9f21-48d8-8ff2-9af68078948f","position":{"commit_sha":"759ee8404cedc58781c7e8b29f1db239555e18ce","position":"1788474792198800271-15d974be-9f21-48d8-8ff2-9af68078948f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"becc896b95e6f38c2675f99f67aa60a264d3d3a93d33f299a54ae83c7c5b84a7","event_uuid":"43e8e59a-2c79-467d-ac37-4740caa86c5f","position":{"commit_sha":"3f5010afed9753f051015d6994eb7621ff87d8fa","position":"1788474946289117332-43e8e59a-2c79-467d-ac37-4740caa86c5f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA (Phase 1 only; no fix landed): The five `test_atomic_completion_close.py` failures are host-harness environment contamination, not a missing `refs/heads/tickets` ref and not a Git 2.55 push/default-branch change. This session inherits `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=3` with `GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0=safe.bareRepository` / `GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0=explicit`, which overrides the user's global `safe.bareRepository=all`. The failing assertions call the test helper `_git(remote, ...)` on a bare fixture remote (`tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py:40-46`, remote created/pushed in `_ticket_remote` at :102-117), and Git refuses that read with `fatal: cannot use bare repository ... (safe.bareRepository is 'explicit')`. Inspection of the failed fixture remotes with `git -c safe.bareRepository=all -C <remote> rev-parse refs/heads/tickets` proves the ref exists. Discriminating experiment: running the same target file with only the injected `GIT_CONFIG_*` entries removed, still using host `git version 2.55.0`, passes: `17 passed in 40.47s`. A minimal Git 2.55 push to a bare remote likewise creates `refs/heads/tickets` when the injected config is absent. CI impact: expected none for Gerrit Verified; `_build-and-test.yml`/`gerrit-verify.yaml` run on `ubuntu-latest`, install Python 3.12/uv, and do not set this Copilot harness `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT` override. Disposition: accepted as environment/config; local full-suite pre-flight in this harness may show this cluster red unless `GIT_CONFIG_*` injection is sanitized or bare-remote test helpers opt in to safe bare access. No code fix landed.","timestamp":1788474792198800271},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA COMPLETE — disposition: ACCEPTED (host-environment artifact, no code fix warranted).\n\nRoot cause: the injected Copilot/Git environment sets GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=3 with KEY_0=safe.bareRepository=explicit (also credential.interactive=never, core.fsmonitor=\"\"). The test helper reads the bare fixture remotes via `git -C <tickets-remote.git> ...`; with safe.bareRepository=explicit git REFUSES to operate on a bare repo discovered via -C, yielding exit 128 (the refs/heads/tickets ref actually exists). Not git 2.55.0 behavior, not origin/main breakage.\n\nProof: with the injected GIT_CONFIG_* removed, the same host+git gives `17 passed`. Neutralizing just the one key also fixes it:\n  env GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=4 GIT_CONFIG_KEY_3=safe.bareRepository GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_3=all PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make test  → 17 passed\n\nCI impact: NONE. Gerrit `Verified` runs on ubuntu-latest without this injected env, so the cluster is green in CI.\n\nGuidance for the janitor epic (78f2): full-suite LOCAL pre-flight on this host must prepend the safe.bareRepository=all override (append as GIT_CONFIG entry #3). This does NOT block landing. No production/test code change required.","timestamp":1788474946289117332}],"created_at":1788474258154670222,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"72f618b9-44ac-44b9-b9a0-62258becfb38","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"b35a-abf6-02fd-4b31"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered while running full `make test` as the local pre-flight for janitor leaf b35a. **Five** tests in `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py` FAIL on a clean checkout of `origin/main` (reproduced in a throwaway worktree at origin/main, freshly `make install`ed), independent of any janitor change:\n\n- test_relevant_remote_rejection_never_places_candidate_on_shared_head\n- test_successful_push_followed_by_remote_rewrite_fails_closed\n- test_unrelated_remote_rejection_merges_and_rebuilds_private_candidate\n- test_lost_push_ack_is_confirmed_without_publishing_a_second_bundle\n- test_post_push_convergence_preserves_concurrent_local_delivery_pending\n\n## Evidence\n\nFailing assertion (representative):\n`assert _git(remote, \"rev-parse\", \"refs/heads/tickets\") == remote_tip` → `git -C <tmp>/tickets-remote.git rev-parse refs/heads/tickets` returns exit 128 (ref does not exist on the fixture bare remote).\n\nEnvironment: git **2.55.0** (very new), init.defaultBranch=main, user set. Fails both in isolation and in-module (5 failed, 12 passed). These are all remote push/rejection/rewrite semantics for the tickets branch.\n\n## Hypothesis to investigate (RCA required, do not fix blind)\n\nCI keeps origin/main green, so either (a) these tests are environment/git-version-sensitive (git 2.55.0 changed push-rejection or default-ref behavior such that the fixture remote never ends up with refs/heads/tickets), or (b) a genuine latent breakage CI doesn't exercise. Classify (a) vs (b), find the true root cause, and determine CI impact.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Root cause identified with a confirmed reproduction and a one-line causal explanation.\n- [ ] Classified: environment/git-version-specific vs genuine main breakage; state whether CI Verified is affected.\n- [ ] If a code/test fix is warranted, it is scoped with file_impact; otherwise an accepted-reason disposition is recorded.\n- [ ] Guidance recorded for the janitor epic on whether full-suite local pre-flight is blocked for all leaves by this cluster.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"740d-187c-53a2-4b7d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Pre-existing: 5 tests in test_atomic_completion_close.py fail locally on origin/main (refs/heads/tickets rev-parse exit 128; git 2.55.0)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["518aa08c-6903-4ea4-8f01-087d1bf2136b","72f618b9-44ac-44b9-b9a0-62258becfb38","15d974be-9f21-48d8-8ff2-9af68078948f","43e8e59a-2c79-467d-ac37-4740caa86c5f"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788474946289117333,"uuid":"21ce85ce-285f-49a3-824f-7d1291c52dd7"}